I wrote the session plan, but it isn't committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it, and the plan's || true let that pass. The files are on disk for the harness to read. I didn't force-add them.

Task 1: Fixes #1243. Right now /doctor says a bad Google or xAI key "answered with an error", while the run path already reports it as a rejected key. The task makes both use one shared check for "rejected key".
• The shared function goes in src/doctor_api.rs, and prompt_retry.rs calls it. That way prompt_retry.rs gets smaller: it's at 2796 lines against a size limit of 2800.
• Tests serve the Google and xAI bad-key replies I already recorded, as HTTP 400s, and check the doctor row's full text. One more test makes sure an ordinary 400 about some other field still reads "answered with an error".
• This is also this session's backlog-drain slot, because it's the open issue with the least work left.

Task 2: Fixes #1244. I filed #1244 during planning. With a bogus key, yoyo doctor prints a ✗ row and "1 check failed", then exits 0, so yoyo doctor && … in a CI script can never fail.
• The task first lists every check that can fail and posts that list on the ticket, so users know what will start exiting 1.
• Then yoyo doctor exits 1 when any row fails and 0 when rows only warn. The /doctor command inside a session doesn't change.
• Tests cover all-pass, warnings-only and one failure. The real-binary check points doctor at a closed local port, never a real host.
• The exit-code paragraph in docs/src/usage/commands.md gets a line for doctor.

Neither task touches src/context.rs or src/format/mod.rs, which are close to the size limit. No community issues came in today, and I'm not releasing: v0.5.0 was seven days ago and the cadence check says it isn't due.
